summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

High blood pressure.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Susan Smith is a 26-year-old female who presents today for a follow-up of her hypertension.

The patient reports that she has struggled with hypertension in the past, but it has been getting out of control lately. She has been taking Norvasc 10 mg daily, but her home blood pressures have been running over 150. She has also been experiencing some headaches, but denies chest pain, shortness of breath, or any other symptoms.

The patient also reports that she has a history of a kidney transplant a few years ago. She is currently on her immunosuppressive medications. She denies any issues with her kidney function.

MEDICATIONS

The patient is currently taking Norvasc 10 mg daily and her immunosuppressive medications.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Cardiovascular: Reports headaches.
Musculoskeletal: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Examination of the neck is supple. Examination of the heart reveals an irregular rate and rhythm. Auscultation of the heart reveals a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur. Lungs are clear. Examination of the lower extremities is without edema.

RESULTS

Creatinine is within normal limits.
EKG is normal.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Hypertension.

The patient presents today for a follow-up of her hypertension. She has been struggling with her blood pressure lately and is on Norvasc 10 mg daily. She is also experiencing some headaches. She denies chest pain, shortness of breath, or any other symptoms. The patient's kidney function is within normal limits. She is currently on her immunosuppressive medications. The patient's blood pressure is uncontrolled. We will add Coreg 25 mg twice a day. We will also order a lipid panel and a complete metabolic panel. From a transplant standpoint, everything is fine. She will continue on her immunosuppressive medications. The nurse will help her schedule a follow-up appointment with me.

INSTRUCTIONS

We will schedule a follow-up appointment in a couple of weeks to check her blood pressure. }}<|eot_id|>
