Irritable Bowel Syndrome with Functional Abdominal Pain, Nausea and Vomiting.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Brittany Edwards is a pleasant 32-year-old female who was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, who was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome. She was prescribed Bentyl, which she uses as needed for intestinal cramping. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, Bentyl up to four times daily for intestinal cramping, and to stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.

The patient reports that she has been going out to eat on Friday nights and Saturday nights and has had some spicy foods or spicy shrimp. She states that she has been having some cramping and nausea. She denies any vomiting.

The patient reports that she has been having a bowel movement 2-3 times a day. She states that they are formed. She notes that after she goes out, she tends to have diarrhea. She states that she is not sure if it is the food or the alcohol or both.

She reports that she usually eats pasta, the chicken alfredo at Friday's restaurant. She notes that it normally does not bother her. She states that she usually drinks tequila or dark liquor. She notes that she prefers Patron. She states that she only gets two drinks every now and then. She notes that if she gets brown liquor, she only gets two. She notes that she will drink a martini sometimes. She states that it is the mixer they put in the drinks that tends to bother her.

The patient reports that when she is not eating out or drinking, what she eats on a daily basis does help her stay regular. When it does flare up, it is not as bad. She notes that she is still having cramping and sharp pains, so she has been avoiding heavy foods. She notes that she did have some fried chicken today.

The patient reports that she has not been taking the Citrucel regularly.

The patient reports that she is having some cramping and nausea. She notes that she is still having diarrhea. She notes that she is avoiding heavy foods. She notes that she had some fried chicken today. She states that she feels like she can not go out without some fried chicken at least once in a while.

