summary is: {{ Hx: 40-year-old female presents with back pain after twisting injury at a birthday party. No radiculopathy, no numbness down legs, some stiffness with rotation. No history of back problems before except for lumbar fusion. No compression fractures on x-ray. 

Imp: Strain of lower back. 

Plan: Ibuprofen 800mg three times a day with food, ice and heat alternating on back, and walking. Follow up in one week if not better. }}<|eot_id|>
