summary is: {{ PC: 27-year-old female, presents with knee pain in the right knee, 2 weeks ago, after increasing swimming activity, breaststroke, with no injury, no trauma, no fever, no chills, no rash, no headache, no vomiting, no diarrhea, no chest pain, no shortness of breath, no cough, no sore throat, no hoarseness, no dysuria, no hematuria, no change in bowel movements, no change in appetite, no change in sleep, no weight loss, no recent travel, no sick contacts, no sick contacts, no recent illness, no recent surgery, no recent hospitalization, no recent medication, no allergies, no PMHx, no SHx, no FHx, no DHx.
Imp: Chondromalacia patellae, secondary to overuse from swimming breaststroke.
Plan: Ibuprofen 600mg 4 times a day, with food, for 2 weeks. Straight leg raising exercises, to strengthen quadriceps. Avoid any activities that puts extra pressure on the knees. If symptoms persist or worsen in 2 weeks, then follow up. 
