summary is: {{ HPC: 33-year-old female, presents with bilateral knee pain, worse on both knees, has been having knee pain after stair workouts, previously had rotator cuff repair 2 years ago. No other joint pain. No pins and needles, swelling in legs. No fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, shortness of breath. Has high blood pressure, on medication, and has been taking it regularly. Has been monitoring blood sugars well.

PMHx: hypertension, rotator cuff repair 2 years ago.

SHx: denies any other joint pain, no pins and needles, swelling in legs. No fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, shortness of breath.

Impression: bilateral knee pain, possible strain, may need to rule out any other conditions. No other joint pain. No pins and needles, swelling in legs. No fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, shortness of breath.

Plan: physical therapy, meloxicam 15mg once a day, autoimmune profile, lipid profile, blood pressure check at home, metformin 500mg twice a day, to continue. }}<|eot_id|>
