summary is: {{ History of present illness: The patient is a 20-year-old female who is being seen for her yearly follow-up for asthma, allergic rhinitis and food allergy. She was switched to wixela due to insurance changes. She has been using it once in the morning and once at night and has not had any issues with it. She has been using zyrtec in the spring, summer and fall for her seasonal allergy symptoms which tend to work well. She has known peanut allergy and is tolerant to almonds and cashews. 
Past medical history: Asthma, allergic rhinitis, food allergy
Past surgical history: None
Medications: wixela, zyrtec, albuterol
Social history: Smokes, vapes. Trying to quit.
Family history: Nil
Social history: Lives at home with her family. Works as a waitress. 
General exam: Normal
Vital signs: BP 120/80, HR 80, RR 16, T 37.1
Dx: Asthma, allergic rhinitis, food allergy
Impression: Asthma, allergic rhinitis, food allergy
Plan: 
1. Continue wixela once in the morning and once at night.
2. Use zyrtec as needed in the spring, summer and fall.
3. Use albuterol as needed.
4. Avoid peanuts and tree nuts.
5. Repeat spirometry in 4 months. 
6. Monitor her asthma control and adjust medications as needed.
7. Follow up with her in 4 months with spirometry. }}<|eot_id|>
