summary is: {{ HPC: 3/2/1972.
Patient: Jordan Roberts.
Chief complaint: Palpitations.
PMHx: Hypertension.
Past medical history: None.
DHx: None.
FHx: Mother and father have hypertension.
SHx: Works as a manager. He drinks 3-4 cups of coffee. No smoking. No drinking.
Imp: BP 146/90, PR 60. Pulse normal. No murmurs. No rubs. Lungs clear. Abdomen normal. Ext normal. No swelling.

Plan: Spironolactone 50mg OD. Continue on hydrochlorothiazide 25mg OD. Continue on amlodipine 10mg OD. Review of DASH diet. Encourage him to reduce his salt intake. Encourage him to walk on the treadmill. Monitor blood pressure and electrolytes in 2 weeks. If not controlled, refer to resistant hypertension clinic. }}<|eot_id|>
