summary is: {{ History of Present Illness: 
The patient is a 32-year-old female who was last seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. She was diagnosed with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) and treated with bentyl. She was instructed to start a low dose fiber supplement, such as citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, bentyl up to four times daily for intestinal cramping, and stop reglan and use zofran as needed. Neuromodulators such as elavil and buspar were discussed but not started. She has been experiencing diarrhea, nausea, and abdominal pain. She has been having bowel movements between two and three times a day, and her stools are formed. She has noticed that after eating spicy foods or drinking, she has diarrhea. She has been experiencing nausea and vomiting. She has had some difficulty with bowel movements on normal days, and her symptoms are worse when she eats spicy foods or drinks.

Physical Examination: 
The patient is alert and cooperative, appears stated age. Her lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. Her heart is regular rate and rhythm. Her abdomen is soft, non-tender, and there is no organomegaly. Her bowel sounds are normal.

Impression: 
The patient has irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting. She has been experiencing diarrhea, nausea, and abdominal pain. She has been having bowel movements between two and three times a day, and her stools are formed. She has noticed that after eating spicy foods or drinking, she has diarrhea. She has been experiencing nausea and vomiting. She has had some difficulty with bowel movements on normal days, and her symptoms are worse when she eats spicy foods or drinks.

Plan: 
I have encouraged dietary and lifestyle modifications, such as reducing greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption. I have started her on elavil 25mg at bedtime for IBS. She can use bentyl 20mg as needed 30-45 minutes prior to eating out at a restaurant. She can also use zofran if needed. I have asked her to follow up in one month by emailing over mychart regarding any side effects and issues, or issues with elavil or if adjustments are needed. }}<|eot_id|>
