summary is: HPC: Patient is a 40-year-old male who presents with a three week history of right upper quadrant abdominal pain. The pain is severe and worsens with fatty food and is associated with nausea and vomiting. He has a history of type 2 diabetes and has been following a keto diet for the past few months. He has had a gallbladder ultrasound that shows multiple gallstones.

Impression: The patient has cholecystitis with gallstones and is at risk of developing complications such as cholangitis and pancreatitis. The patient has not had any improvement in his symptoms with dietary modifications and has had a worsening of his symptoms over the past few weeks. He has had a laparoscopic cholecystectomy scheduled.

Plan: The patient will have a laparoscopic cholecystectomy to remove the gallbladder. He will be admitted to the hospital for postoperative care and will be monitored for any complications. He will be advised to avoid high fat foods and to eat foods that are high in fiber. He will be followed up in clinic in a week to ensure that he is recovering well from the surgery. He will also be advised to follow up with his primary care physician to monitor his type 2 diabetes. }}<|eot_id|>
