summary is: {{ HPC: 31-year-old female with a history of type two diabetes and asthma presents with a week-long history of worsening abdominal pain. She reports increasing pain in the upper abdomen with nausea and vomiting, and also notes worsening pain with exercise. She has been drinking a lot of coffee and has had some recent changes in her diet. She is having a grade three systolic ejection murmur on her physical exam. She has no fever. She has mild tenderness in the epigastrium of her abdomen, but no significant tenderness in the right lower or upper quadrants. She has mild end-expiratory wheezes on lung exam. She has a history of heavy alcohol use and has been drinking a lot of coffee lately. She has no other medical history. She has been taking metformin 500mg twice daily and has been controlling her blood sugars well. She has been taking flovent 250mcg twice daily for her asthma and has not had any recent asthma attacks. She has not had any recent asthma attacks. Impression: gastritis. Plan: to cut back on coffee and alcohol. To take zantac 150mg twice daily. To continue metformin 1000mg in the morning and 500mg in the evening. To continue flovent 250mcg twice daily and albuterol as needed. To follow up in four weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
